@page "/community"

<Seo Canonical="/community" Title="Blazorise Community license retirement" Description="Community applications and renewals are closed. Existing licenses remain valid under their original terms until their current expiration date." />

<Div Class="b-visual b-marketing b-expanded-page">
    <MarketingPageHeader Variant="BrandBackdropVariant.CircleScatter" Counterpoint="BrandBackdropVariant.CircleScatter">
        <Title>The Community license<br /><Span>has been retired.</Span></Title>
        <Description>We no longer accept Community applications or renewals. Your approved license remains valid under its original terms until its current expiration date.</Description>
        <Actions>
            <Anchor To="indie" Class="b-visual-button b-visual-button-primary">Explore Indie</Anchor>
            <Anchor To="docs/start" Class="b-visual-button b-visual-button-outline">Get started</Anchor>
        </Actions>
    </MarketingPageHeader>
    <Container Padding="Padding.Is5.OnY">
        <Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is2">When your Community license expires</Heading>
        <Paragraph>
            To continue using Blazorise without evaluation limits after your license expires, choose <Anchor To="indie">Indie</Anchor> if your project qualifies, or <Anchor To="pricing">compare the other plans</Anchor>.
        </Paragraph>
        <Paragraph>
            While your license is valid, your application continues to display the compact <Strong>Community License</Strong> notice. The <Anchor To="docs/usage/licensing">licensing guide</Anchor> explains how the product token works.
        </Paragraph>
        <Heading Size="HeadingSize.Is2">Starting a new project</Heading>
        <Paragraph>
            Professional and Enterprise cover unlimited projects per licensed developer and include dedicated support. For one developer building an independently owned product, <Anchor To="indie">Indie</Anchor> offers annual project licensing subject to its eligibility requirements. Compare <Anchor To="pricing">plans and benefits</Anchor> before purchasing.
        </Paragraph>
    </Container>
</Div>